slots as slot wrappers; the value and the type it was found on."] [129 1 "// The type attribute cache (PY6-core, queue 200, after PY8's measurement: lookupAttr was 31-35% of a run;"] [130 1 "// CPython's method cache over tp_version_tag): each type keeps its lookups' answers by name, the absent ones"] [131 1 "// too, and drops them all when typeEpoch moves. typeEpoch moves on any change to a type's namespace (the dicts"] [132 1 "// marked ofType: an insertion, a replaced value, a deletion, a clear, popitem), on a getset added, and on an"] [133 1 "// MRO set (c3MRO's and readyTypes'), so an answer is never older than the namespaces it was read from."] [141 1 "// lookupAttrMRO is _PyType_Lookup's walk: t's MRO's dicts, then the getsets and slot wrappers of each."] [162 1 "// superLookup is lookupAttr over the part of start's MRO after typ (super's lookup)."] [191 1 "// descrGet is a found attribute's __get__ (obj nil: from the class); a built-in method found on a"] [192 1 "// built-in type is bound to obj (its value for a built-in subclass's instance)."] [198 3 "// object's methods take the instance itself (PY6d's REQUEST: __reduce_ex__'s class); objectDescr is"] [199 3 "// methodDescrs[b] == ObjectType without the map's lookup on every method's binding (queue 210)"] [211 1 "// methodDescrs are the built-in types' methods that left their type's dict through the class (T.name: CPython's"] [212 1 "// method_descriptor), each with its type: put in a class's dict (socket.socket.getsockname = saved, test_socket's"] [213 1 "// test_injected_authentication_failure) such a method still binds to the instance, as a method descriptor does,"] [214 1 "// where a built-in function there (class A: f = len) does not."] [219 1 "// instanceDict is o's __dict__, nil when it has none."] [246 18 "// queue 304: a property subclass's instance"] [260 1 "// InstanceDictHook is the __dict__ of an object of another package (arbace/pyctypes' C-born objects whose type has a"] [261 1 "// tp_dictoffset: the dict their memory holds; queue 268), nil when it has none."] [264 1 "// The attribute instructions' inline caches (202b; PEP 659's LOAD_ATTR and STORE_ATTR caches, after the type"] [265 1 "// version tag): load-attr and store-attr of an object whose type takes the generic path keep, per instruction, the"] [266 1 "// type they last saw and lookupAttr's answer for it, valid while typeEpoch has not moved (the epoch the type"] [267 1 "// attribute cache's own answers hold by, attr.go's lookupAttr), so a hit compares two words where lookupAttr hashes"] [268 1 "// the name into the type's cache."] [274 2 "// di: where the instance's dict held the name when it was last found there (queue 210; CPython's"] [275 2 "// LOAD_ATTR_INSTANCE_VALUE's index): an entry holding the name's very str (co_names are interned) is the name's"] [279 1 "// lookupAttrAt is lookupAttr(tp, name) through the cache of c's instruction pc."] [285 1 "// attrSite is an instruction's caches: the last types it saw, the latest first (queue 210: richards' four task"] [286 1 "// classes share their methods' instructions, and one entry missed at every change of type)."] [291 1 "// attrSites are every code's inline caches (queue 241), swept by gc.collect: an entry whose epoch is past holds a type"] [292 1 "// and the value found, which CPython's caches (a version tag) do not keep alive (WeakMethod's test_method_dead: the"] [293 1 "// method deleted from its class stays in the site that loaded it). attrSwept is the epoch of the last sweep."] [299 1 "// sweepAttrSites clears the stale entries of every inline cache, once per type epoch."] [316 1 "// attrICAt is c's instruction pc's cache entry holding lookupAttr(tp, name)."] [339 34 "// tp's old entry, else the oldest, dropped"] [344 1 "// dictEntryAt is the position of the entry of d holding name itself, through the hint *di (kept up to date); -1"] [345 1 "// when d does not hold name (an equal str in its place is found, but not kept as the hint)."] [357 1 "// loadAttrAt is load-attr at c's instruction pc: GetAttr, its generic path's lookup through the instruction's cache."] [366 3 "// genericGetAttrFound's instance dict through the hint (queue 210)"] [388 1 "// storeAttrAt is store-attr (v nil: delete-attr) at c's instruction pc: SetAttr, its generic path's lookup through"] [389 1 "// the instruction's cache."] [398 3 "// genericSetAttrFound's dict.Set through the hint: a value replaced in place (queue 210)"] [401 5 "// store_instance_attr's MODIFIED, the value the same or not (queue 274)"] [411 21 "// the usual case: the name inserted last"] [418 1 "// GenericGetAttr is object.__getattribute__."] [425 1 "// genericGetAttrFound is GenericGetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [443 1 "// GenericSetAttr is object.__setattr__ (v nil: object.__delattr__)."] [450 1 "// genericSetAttrFound is GenericSetAttr with lookupAttr's answer for o's type tp."] [478 1 "// typeGetAttr is type.__getattribute__: the metatype's data descriptors, then the type's MRO, then"] [479 1 "// the metatype's other attributes."] [489 3 "// _PyType_Lookup of t's MRO assigns the version tag a watched modification clears (queue 274); the"] [490 3 "// metatype's data descriptors (__name__, __dict__) answer before it"] [497 29 "// a method descriptor leaving its type"] [505 4 "// a built-in type's class and static methods know their type for __qualname__"] [528 1 "// typeSetAttr is type.__setattr__: a class's attribute, its slots updated for a special one."] [539 3 "// tp_name: a static type's module and name ('compression.zstd.ZstdCompressor'; builtins' bare), a frozen class's"] [540 3 "// name (queue 270b: PyType_Freeze)"] [559 26 "// a C type's slots are its own (queue 270b: its dict changes alone)"] [562 19 "// type_setattro's PyType_Modified: the type watchers (queue 274)"] [567 1 "// SetAttr is setattr(o, name, v); v nil is delattr."] [575 1 "// DelAttr is delattr(o, name)."] [578 1 "// GetAttrOptional is getattr(o, name) with nil, not an AttributeError, when there is no such attribute."] [581 1 "// LookupSpecial is a special method's lookup on o's type (_PyObject_LookupSpecial): bound to o, or nil."] [590 1 "// getAttrOptional is getattr(o, name, None) without the None: nil when there is no such attribute."] [602 1 "// callBound calls a method found on self's type bound to self (CPython's vectorcall of an unbound"] [603 1 "// method with self first, or __get__ then the call); owner is the type of self's MRO it was found on"] [604 1 "// (lookupAttr's), nil when not known."] [611 4 "// wrapperdescr_call's check (bpo-37619: a wrapper of the wrong class in a class's dict)"] [617 4 "// a built-in function in a class's dict is no method descriptor: called without the instance, as"] [618 4 "// descrGet's rule and lookup_maybe_method (class C: __call__ = len; typing.NewType's __call__ = _idfunc,"] [619 4 "// queue 207)"] [623 4 "// object's own methods take the instance itself (descrGet's rule, PY6d's R2), as for"] [624 4 "// object.__reduce_ex__ of a class deriving from a built-in type (PY6g's F2: random.Random's pickling)"] [680 2 "// a descriptor's own attributes (PY6a: inspect's getattr_static reads __name__ and __objclass__)"] [701 2 "// object's attributes"] [703 2 "// a built-in type with a dictionary shows it itself (BaseException's, function's, module's); a class's is"] [704 2 "// subtype_getsets_full's, in the dict of the class that adds it (addLayoutDescrs): object has none"] [712 2 "// BaseException's attributes (exceptions.c's BaseException_getset and members)"] [771 1 "// unpackAll is the items of an iterable."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[76 32] [80 32] [119 31] [146 31] [150 28] [154 35] [166 6] [166 20] [172 9] [172 23] [175 31] [179 28] [183 35] [194 26] [205 33] [308 28] [325 23] [347 18] [365 27] [373 41] [397 27] [399 21] [407 32] [410 34] [431 28] [454 34] [493 33] [494 27] [508 34] [512 34] [517 34] [534 35] [555 38] [569 32] [631 33] [652 18] [688 26]